          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: экология",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "экология (ekológiya) — \"ecology, the environment\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Мой брат изучает экологию. Moy brat izucháyet ekológiyu. My brother studies ecology."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine. In everyday speech, the state of the environment: плохая экология (ekológiya)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "экология (ekológiya) is usually traced to German Ökologie, a learned coinage from Greek oîkos \"a house, a household\" and lógos \"word, study\": the study of the home we live in."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
